<newsitem itemid="173822" id="root" date="1996-11-07" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Staveley pretax profits rise in half year.</title>
<headline>Staveley pretax profits rise in half year.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 28</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		  6.7		  vs   5.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	   2.5		  vs   2.3</p>
<p> Pretax			10.2		  vs   8.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   199.1		  vs 174.2</p>
<p> Operating result	  11.5		  vs  10.0</p>
<p> Interest		     1.3		  vs   1.8</p>
<p> Tax			    2.4		  vs   2.0</p>
<p> Pay date		   Jan 7, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  Nov 26</p>
<p>NOTE - Staveley Industries Plc said strong order books and benefits from the reorganisation of Chronos Richardson should enable it to make further progress in the second half.</p>
<p>The company also announced that it has bought two U.S. businesses, Accurate Metallurgical and PCMS, which will be integrated in Conam, part of the Staveley Services Group, for $4.9 million in cash.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
